    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0722" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1947v02/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW (Peace)/10–2047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gallman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-20T18:00:00+01:00">October 20, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5612. We have discussed with Foreign Office German officials Urtel 4452, October 15<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d250-f1"/> and they have today recommended to Foreign Secretary
                        Bevin acceptance US views on basis
                    discussion early November London by US-UK-French experts (1) tactics to take
                    with USSR and (2) actual terms of offer.</p>
                <pb facs="0723" n="689" xml:id="pg689"/>
                <p>If Bevin approves, instructions will be
                    sent British Embassy Washington to contact Department in matter. At this stage
                    Foreign Office feels it will be necesary to bargain with USSR rather than to
                    present it with precise exact offer in monetary terms. Officials also hold view
                    Soviets not likely to be willing to come to settlement during CFM or deputies meeting. However, they agree effort
                    should be made and that “US paper provides satisfactory basis for discussion by
                    experts”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
